      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c021357a58d0a7e70c3e515|full_name}: This is in fact not intended behavior as I have been told. Even if it would be intended behavior, the percent counter is lower or higher depending on how slow or fast a world downloaded. In my case, downloading the world from a local in-house CloudFront cache server causes the world to download very fast and thus the percentage counter almost always stays below 40%.",
